Description: pvr: add VK_EXT_pipeline_robustness
 Advertise VK_EXT_pipeline_robustness with pipelineRobustness and take the
 buffer robustness of each shader stage from vk_pipeline_robustness_state_fill()
 instead of the device-wide robustBufferAccess feature:
 pco_common_data::robust_buffer_access is set when uniform or storage buffers
 of the stage are robust, and the new robust_vertex_inputs selects the robust
 vertex attribute PDS program. Without a VkPipelineRobustnessCreateInfo the
 device default applies, so behaviour is unchanged for applications that do not
 use the extension. The default robustness properties are DISABLED, which is
 what the driver does when no robustness feature is enabled.
 .
 zink (patches 0048-0052, from Mesa main) then disables the device-wide
 robustness features and requests robustness only for pipelines of robust GL
 contexts, so the bounds checks on every UBO/SSBO access go away for ordinary
 GL applications.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
